# x-residual-moves-b-client: core lines for the two blob-carrying methods

The desktop sends the data of `desktop/userFile/write` ("Save as", up to a 64 MiB data URL) and `desktop/attachment/write` (an attachment
opened from the chat) as blobs (`blob/put` chunks, then `{ "$blobRef": digest, "as": ... }`), as every listed field larger than one inbound
frame must. Without the lines below the app server refuses the reference with `invalidParams`.

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-app-protocol/src/boundary/blob_fields.json (hot: protocol)
Add under "methods" (after "git/applyPatch"):

    "desktop/attachment/write": ["/dataUrl"],
    "desktop/userFile/write": ["/dataBase64"]

(apps/desktop/src/shared/core-lanes/blob-ref-fields.ts gets the same two rows: see apps/desktop/pending-wire/x-residual-moves-b-client.wire.)

## 2. mixdog-core-domains domains/blob/param_refs.rs, `expansion_bound`
A "Save as" source is at most 64 MiB of characters (`requiredSaveSource`), the base64 of the file; the default bound is 32 MB. Add an arm before `_`:

    "desktop/userFile/write" => 64 * 1024 * 1024,

(The `dataUrl` of `desktop/attachment/write` stays within the default.)

## 3. SERVICE_PENDING
Nothing: the nine `desktop/*` names of DesktopResidualBService left it in G7-WIRE.
